{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 4, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie is directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his quick-witted dialogue and fast-paced storytelling.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard university, who is dumped by his girlfriend erica albright (played by rooney mara). this event sets off a chain reaction that leads to the creation of a website called \"facemash,\" which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and attention from the university administration. mark is then approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are members of the rowing team and want mark to help them create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students.\n\nmark agrees to help the winklevoss twins, but instead uses their idea to create his own site, thefacebook, with the help of his friend eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield). the site quickly gains popularity and spreads to other colleges and universities.\n\nas thefacebook grows in popularity, mark and eduardo become more and more successful, but their friendship begins to deteriorate. meanwhile, the winklevoss twins and their friend divya narendra (played by max minghella) become increasingly frustrated with mark's actions and decide to sue him for stealing their idea.\n\nthe film's narrative is presented through a series of flashbacks, as mark is deposed in the lawsuits brought against him by the winklevoss twins and eduardo. the depositions provide a framework for the story, and allow the audience to see the events of the film from different perspectives.\n\nthe social network features a talented cast, with standout performances from jesse eisenberg and andrew garfield. eisenberg's portrayal of mark zuckerberg is particularly impressive, as he brings a sense of intensity and focus to the role. the film's cinematography is also noteworthy, with a muted color palette that reflects the dark and moody tone of the story.\n\none of the most striking aspects of the social network is its score, which was composed by trent reznor and atticus ross. the music is haunting and atmospheric, and perfectly captures the sense of unease and tension that pervades the film.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-crafted and engaging film that explores the complexities of friendship, ambition, and the consequences of success. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story of facebook and the people behind it.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11627468466758728}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.6927862816373818e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.033068470656871796}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.3828373084834311e-05}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.24969758093357086}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.052504830062389374}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.16264863312244415}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -7.152560215217818e-07}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -8.821526535029989e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -4.529963462118758e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.04119579493999481}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.01702679507434368}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005529859336093068}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00015569945389870554}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0788910835981369}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00019152805907651782}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.08090510964393616}, {"token": " lawsuits", "logprob": -0.11771067976951599}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0017444200348109007}, {"token": " followed", "logprob": -0.0040954058058559895}, {"token": "."